I've fixed the build errors and left out the enrichment fetch. This node's authority is only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`. A request to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would need `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node was not granted. Adding that import would also send the input's text to an outside host. If the enrichment is needed, the graph's `with` clause would have to grant an `HTTPClient` scoped to that host.

The build failed because `AgentResponse`, `LlmError` and `Intent` are not named by the export. wit-bindgen therefore generates them under `crate::aap::caps::types`, not at the crate root, so `src/lib.rs` now imports them from there.

